From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: dxgi: swap chains for composition

IDXGIFactory2::CreateSwapChainForComposition was a stub. WebView2's GPU
process makes one for every WebView (Chromium's software output device on
the swap-chain path) and, when it fails, restarts itself for "context loss"
until it gives up: the page loads, its script runs, and nothing is ever
shown.

A composition swap chain has no window. DirectComposition shows it as the
content of a visual, and tells it, through the new private interface
IWineDXGICompositionSwapChain, which window its visual tree is bound to and
at what offset (patch 0191).

Direct3D 11 devices only. The back buffer is an ordinary texture that
persists across presents; Present reads it back and draws it into the
target window with GDI. With no compositor, the host window (in WebView2,
in another process) may paint over the frame at any time, so the last frame
is drawn again 100 ms after each present and every 500 ms after that.

--- a/include/wine/winedxgi.idl
+++ b/include/wine/winedxgi.idl
@@ -87,6 +87,18 @@
     HRESULT get_adapter_info([out] struct wine_dxgi_adapter_info *info);
 }
 
+/* A swap chain made by CreateSwapChainForComposition: DirectComposition
+ * tells it which window shows it, and where, when its visual is committed. */
+[
+    object,
+    local,
+    uuid(7c3f5d2e-9a41-4b8e-b6d3-2f0e8a1c5b94)
+]
+interface IWineDXGICompositionSwapChain : IUnknown
+{
+    HRESULT set_target([in] HWND window, [in] int x, [in] int y);
+}
+
